Track 2: Did the Larva Feel the Sun?
- Story & Context: Taped in the claustrophobic attic of 18th Street during an August heatwave, this track served as Anya Chen's taped confession regarding the incomplete automaton chassis she sheltered behind her water heater for six months before the city inspectors seized it. To recreate the sound of the machine's rattling internal fan, Maya bowed her slide guitar across a saturated tape loop while Bo breathed an aching, circular drone that rattled the cheap linoleum floor. Anya wept quietly between vocal takes into an unshielded condenser mic coated in sticky salt spray, finally delivering the hook "you won't rust if you keep singing" as bright steel-pan arpeggios bloomed through the haze.
